From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Proton GE Team <proton-ge@example.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 02:05:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Report live source ranges compatibly.

IMFMediaSource::GetCharacteristics() returns MFMEDIASOURCE_* flags, but
GetSeekable() tested the result with the unrelated MFBYTESTREAM_IS_SEEKABLE
flag.  Its value aliases MFMEDIASOURCE_CAN_PAUSE, so every pausable live
source was incorrectly exposed as seekable.

Unknown-duration live HLS sources use positive infinity for their media
duration. Media Engine clients such as AVPro use the synthetic buffered and
seekable ranges as live-presentation readiness signals. Preserve the existing
[0, +infinity] ranges for live sources; returning an empty range leaves AVPro
polling those properties until its own playback timeout even after decoded
frames and the PLAYING event are available.
---
 dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -2518,9 +2518,10 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_GetSeekable(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface, IMFMedia
     {
         hr = create_time_range(&time_range);
         if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && !isnan(engine->duration) && engine->presentation.source)
         {
             hr = IMFMediaSource_GetCharacteristics(engine->presentation.source, &flags);
-            if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && (flags & MFBYTESTREAM_IS_SEEKABLE))
+            if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && (isinf(engine->duration)
+                    || (flags & MFMEDIASOURCE_CAN_SEEK)))
                 hr = IMFMediaTimeRange_AddRange(time_range, 0.0, engine->duration);
         }
     }
